description:
Add or replace a Code component — JavaScript that runs in the browser and makes a project DO something. It runs on ONE event you choose (`event`): RENDER_BEFORE (default) every frame, for movement (held keys: this.keysPressed); KEY_DOWN / KEY_UP once per press / release; MOUSE_CLICK, SWIPE, MUSIC_BEAT, PHYSICS_COLLISION once per click, swipe, beat, collision. A script per event: r3_docs_read("HOWTO_CODE_EVENTS.md"). Kept at once in the project's live copy: every R3 tab with the project open gets the new code now, no editor needed and nothing to save (r3_editor_code is the same tool). The answer says what was kept, its seq and codeVersion.

Call r3_project_load FIRST: code addresses components by their entityRef, and that tool tells you those names. Read r3_docs_read("CODE_PATTERNS.md") before your first Code component: a guessed API saves and then silently does nothing.

HOW TO WRITE IT — a function body that RETURNS its hooks:
```js
this.start = function() {
  // once, when the code starts
};
this.update = function(data) {
  this['mesh_cube_1'].rotation.y += data.delta;
};
return {start: this.start, update: this.update};   // REQUIRED — nothing runs without it
```
Reach any component with `this['<entityRef>']`, and the project's infrastructure with this.getProject() / getScene() / getCamera() / getRenderer() / getWorld() / getAudioListener() / getEntityInstance(), never a guessed ref. Anything else you return is an api other scripts call: `this['<entityRef>'].api.<name>(...)`.

There is NO getComponentByRef, no this.state, no this.getSibling and no R3 global: code using them is REFUSED, not saved.

EVENTS (by NAME; default RENDER_BEFORE): RENDER_BEFORE, RENDER_AFTER, KEY_DOWN, KEY_UP, MOUSE_DOWN, MOUSE_UP, MOUSE_MOVE, MOUSE_WHEEL, MOUSE_CLICK, TOUCH_START, TOUCH_MOVE, TOUCH_END, TOUCH_CANCEL, SWIPE, MUSIC_BEAT, MUSIC_BAR, PHYSICS_COLLISION. Their `data` (mouse: nested, -1..+1): the how-to's table.

Pass entityRef + baseVersion (the codeVersion r3_code_read gave) to REPLACE a script (and its event); name (or neither) to create one. Code is never merged: a write on an older version is refused with the current code.
